SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Democratic Republic of the Congo: Freedom in the World 2023 Country Report","publisher":"Freedom House","publication_date":"2023-01-01","url":"https://freedomhouse.org/country/democratic-republic-congo/freedom-world/2023","claim":"Freedom House says the DRC's political system is paralyzed by manipulation of the electoral process by political elites, and that opposition parties and civil society frequently criticize CENI and the Constitutional Court for lacking independence.","locator":"Overview and A3 sections","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent country report with explicit electoral-process and institutional-independence findings relevant to 2022.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Retrospective 2022 country assessment","ruler_attribution":"Structural under Tshisekedi's administration, though not all defects are personally ordered by him.","contrary_evidence":["The same report notes some opposition members were released and some exiles returned under Tshisekedi."],"lenses":["4B.1","4B.2","4B.4","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Democratic Republic of the Congo: Freedom in the World 2023 Country Report","publisher":"Freedom House","publication_date":"2023-01-01","url":"https://freedomhouse.org/country/democratic-republic-congo/freedom-world/2023","claim":"Freedom House reports that in August 2022 opposition leader Jean-Marc Kabund, formerly an ally of President Tshisekedi, was arrested for allegedly insulting the president after launching a new opposition party in July.","locator":"Key Developments in 2022","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent country report with a dated 2022 arrest tied to opposition activity.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 political-repression incident","ruler_attribution":"Directly relevant to Tshisekedi-era treatment of a breakaway opposition figure.","contrary_evidence":["The report does not by itself prove a presidential order; it documents the arrest as a political event."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.5","4B.8","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"République démocratique du Congo 2022 - EN","publisher":"RSF","publication_date":"2022-01-01","url":"https://rsf.org/en/analyse_regionale/627","claim":"RSF says the national broadcaster RTNC lacks independence, local authorities commonly pressure journalists and media outlets, and the press law is obsolete and oppressive with prisons terms still attached to press offences.","locator":"Media landscape, political context, and legal framework sections","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent press-freedom monitor with direct country-level assessment of media control and legal pressure.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 media environment and inherited legal framework","ruler_attribution":"Relevant to the Tshisekedi administration's media environment and tolerance of independent information.","contrary_evidence":["RSF also notes the authorities had committed to overhaul the press law, so the record includes stated reform intent."],"lenses":["4B.6","4B.9","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"World Report 2022: Democratic Republic of Congo","publisher":"Human Rights Watch","publication_date":"2022-01-01","url":"https://www.hrw.org/world-report/2022/country-chapters/democratic-republic-congo","claim":"HRW says journalists, activists, whistleblowers, and critics of government policy were intimidated, threatened, beaten, arrested, and in some cases prosecuted by authorities and security forces; it also says supporters of Tshisekedi's UDPS attacked Catholic churches and priests over an independent electoral-commission push.","locator":"Freedom of Expression, Peaceful Assembly, and Media section; 2021 background retained in 2022 report","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent rights report tying repression and party-aligned intimidation to the ruling environment.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Transition into 2022 and inherited political-environment baseline","ruler_attribution":"Relevant to Tshisekedi's political environment and party ecosystem, but not every incident is a direct presidential order.","contrary_evidence":["The same report also notes a transitional-justice commission and limited accountability steps in 2021-2022."],"lenses":["4B.2","4B.3","4B.4","4B.5","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"DR Congo: Martial Law Brings Crackdown in East","publisher":"Human Rights Watch","publication_date":"2022-03-22","url":"https://www.hrw.org/news/2022/03/22/dr-congo-martial-law-brings-crackdown-east","claim":"HRW says the military and police curtailed freedom of expression, used lethal force against peaceful demonstrations, and arbitrarily detained and prosecuted activists, journalists, and political opposition members under martial law in North Kivu and Ituri.","locator":"news report body around lines 616-620","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Detailed independent investigation with direct attribution to the martial-law governance structure under Tshisekedi.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 domestic political-repression context","ruler_attribution":"Directly relevant because Tshisekedi's administration maintained the state of siege and set its duration.","contrary_evidence":["HRW notes the government justified martial law as an anti-insecurity measure and the report is focused on abuse allegations."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.5","4B.8","4B.9","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"La Feuille de route et ses préalables","publisher":"CENI","publication_date":"2022-02-03","url":"https://www.ceni.cd/index.php/communique-de-presse/2022/02/03/la-feuille-de-route-et-ses-prealables","claim":"CENI's 2022 roadmap says its electoral work faced major politico-security, financial, legal, technical, logistical, and sanitary constraints and that the institution had weak logistical capacity.","locator":"paragraphs 98-104","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary electoral-authority statement on the practical constraints facing the 2022-2023 electoral process.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Direct 2022 election-preparation context","ruler_attribution":"Institutional context under Tshisekedi rather than proof of his personal intent.","contrary_evidence":["The same source frames these as challenges to overcome, not excuses to abandon the process."],"lenses":["4B.1","4B.2","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Élections en RDC : Présidentielle, législatives nationales et provinciales fixées au 20 décembre 2023, voici toutes les dates","publisher":"Actualite.cd","publication_date":"2022-11-26","url":"https://actualite.cd/index.php/2022/11/26/elections-en-rdc-presidentielle-legislatives-nationales-et-provinciales-fixees-au-20","claim":"The CENI set the presidential, legislative, and provincial elections for 20 December 2023, and the report says many feared a constitutional-delay 'glissement' because of the accumulated delay.","locator":"article lines 109-112","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous local reporting of the election calendar and the risk of constitutional delay.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Year-end 2022 election-calendar milestone","ruler_attribution":"Relevant to Tshisekedi's record because the 2022 calendar governed the run-up to the next contest.","contrary_evidence":["Publishing a calendar is not the same as delivering a fair election or proving democratic commitment."],"lenses":["4B.1","4B.8","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"RDC: Jean Marc Kabund arrêté","publisher":"Actualite.cd","publication_date":"2022-08-09","url":"https://actualite.cd/2022/08/09/rdc-jean-marc-kabund-arrete","claim":"Actualite.cd reports that Jean-Marc Kabund was arrested on 9 August 2022, transferred to Makala prison, and that a police official said he had received an order to take Kabund there after the second audition.","locator":"article lines 93-97","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous local-language reporting with direct procedural details and named actors.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 opposition-arrest episode","ruler_attribution":"Directly relevant to the Tshisekedi-era treatment of a former party insider turned opposition figure.","contrary_evidence":["The article describes a judicial process and does not by itself prove presidential direction of the arrest."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.8","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"RDC: Kabund arrêté pour 'outrage au chef de l’État, imputations dommageables et diffamation'","publisher":"Actualite.cd","publication_date":"2022-08-09","url":"https://actualite.cd/index.php/2022/08/09/rdc-kabund-arrete-pour-outrage-au-chef-de-letat-imputations-dommageables-et-diffamation","claim":"The AFP/Actualite report says Kabund was arrested in Kinshasa and charged with outrage against the head of state, harmful imputations, and defamation after he publicly denounced Tshisekedi's camp and launched his own party.","locator":"article lines 89-101","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous wire-report corroboration with the charge language and political context spelled out.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 repression and opposition-control episode","ruler_attribution":"Directly relevant to Tshisekedi's political-space record.","contrary_evidence":["The article also records criticism that the arrest could compromise free and credible 2023 elections."],"lenses":["4B.2","4B.3","4B.5","4B.8","4B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"RDC : JED dénonce la flambée des attaques contre les médias depuis les Etats généraux de la presse","publisher":"Actualite.cd","publication_date":"2022-05-02","url":"https://actualite.cd/index.php/2022/05/02/rdc-jed-denonce-la-flambee-des-attaques-contre-les-medias-depuis-les-etats-generaux-de","claim":"JED said it had recorded 75 press-freedom violations by early May 2022, including 19 journalist arrests and 11 media closures, and that Tshisekedi had promised to accompany decriminalization of press offenses and guarantee media independence.","locator":"article lines 95-101 and 116-118","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous report quoting JED's annual observation and the president's pledge at the press conference.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 press-freedom context","ruler_attribution":"Directly relevant to Tshisekedi's media-treatment record and reform commitments.","contrary_evidence":["The same item notes a presidential commitment to reform, so the evidence is mixed rather than uniformly negative."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.6","4B.10"]}

Search ledger:
- Candidate documents found: about 24 in this pass.
- Documents opened: 11 accessible documents plus several find views on already opened pages.
- Duplicate families removed: 8.
- Irrelevant or out-of-period items culled: 5.
- Inaccessible items: 6.
- Accepted distinct new URLs: 8.

Material gaps:
- I still do not have a clean primary 2022 source on CENI independence, Constitutional Court behavior, or any formal anti-capture reform actually implemented by Tshisekedi.
- The strongest 2022 pattern is negative: state-of-siege repression, journalist pressure, and opposition arrests.
- The clearest positive evidence is procedural, not substantive: election scheduling and stated reform intent.
- I did not find a 2022 observer report for the later presidential ballot because that ballot was still in preparation during the target year.

Next best directions:
1. Pull the full CENI 2022 electoral roadmap PDF and any 2022 amendments to the electoral law.
2. Pull direct Constitutional Court or parliamentary records on appointments, rulings, or election-related disputes in 2022.
3. Pull the JED 2022 annual report PDF and any human-rights-commission report on press arrests and protest policing.
4. Pull CENCO/ECC, EU, or AU statements on the 2022 election calendar and institutional independence.
5. If you want a tighter 4B.9 sub-dossier, add direct 2022 provincial orders on media suspension or internet/digital restrictions.
